Hi [~accountid:6151cf6878e5e40070fb74c2],

Please find below the answers to your questions:

*1.Is the market subject to laws where an employment relationship can be deemed or implied? yes/no.* 

{color:#bf2600}Yes. {color}

{color:#bf2600}For context, in Spain there are two types of drivers: i) independent drivers and ii) fleet drivers.{color}

* {color:#bf2600}The independent drivers are self-employed drivers who provide the transportation services with their own vehicles and administrative license through the Bolt app. {color}
* {color:#bf2600}Fleet drivers are employees of a company (a fleet). This company  provides transportation services through the Bolt app hiring drivers for this purpose. This company that holds the administrative license and owns the vehicles is the one that maintains a commercial relationship with Bolt.{color}

{color:#bf2600}As for the independent drivers, Labour Courts consider that individuals entering into a relationship with digital platforms for providing transport  services with their own vehicles and administrative licenses, in principle, must not be considered employees but self employed workers. Therefore, in principle, t{color}{color:#bf2600}*here are no reclassification risks when it comes to independent drivers.*{color}

{color:#bf2600}However, when it comes to fleet drivers, according to article 43 Statue of Workers ({color}{color:#bf2600}*“SW”*{color}{color:#bf2600}) {color}{color:#bf2600}*it will be considered that there is an illegal assignment of employees if certain circumstances concur*{color}{color:#bf2600}. Please see question 3 for further details.{color}

*2. Is there any evidence that platforms are under scrutiny under the legal system (litigation etc).* 

{color:#bf2600}In the last years, there has been many cases brought to Spanish Courts by drivers alleging that their employers (i.e. the fleets) illegally assign them to the owners of digital platforms. These cases have had different outcomes, depending on the individual circumstances of each case.{color}

*3. Is the relevant test subject to express presumption criteria? yes/no* 

{color:#bf2600}Yes, according to article 43 of SW, it will be considered that there is an illegal assignment of employees when any or all of the following circumstances arise: {color}

* {color:#bf2600}The purpose of service contracts between Bolt and the fleet is limited to the mere secondment of the fleet's workers to Bolt.{color}
* {color:#bf2600}The fleet does not have its own stable activity or organization, nor does it have the necessary means to carry out its activity.{color}
* {color:#bf2600}The fleet does not exercise the functions inherent to its status as employer.{color}

{color:#bf2600}Please note that if a Court finds that any of the above circumstances have arisen, the consequence would be as follows:{color}

* {color:#bf2600}The fleet and Bolt shall be jointly and severally liable for the obligations towards the employees and the Social Security.{color}
* {color:#bf2600}The unlawfully assigned employees would be entitled to be considered permanent employees of either the fleet or Bolt.{color}
* {color:#bf2600}Both the fleet and Bolt may be imposed fines ranging from EUR 7,501 to EUR 225,018.{color}

*4. Are reclassification sensitive activity expressly considered by a court or any law to imply an employment relationship?* 

{color:#bf2600}See the answer above.{color}

*5. Can claims be made in respect of past periods (i.e. for previously withheld earnings?)*

{color:#bf2600}If what is to be claimed is the  the status of employee, the claim of illegal assignment must be filed when the illegal assignment occurs, or when a dismissal takes place.{color}

{color:#bf2600}However, the Supreme Court ruling of 29 June 2022 says that it is not required that the situation of assignment subsists at the time of filing the claim, if what is being claimed is another right, such as the calculation of the period in which there was an illegal assignment for the purposes of seniority.{color}

*6. Who is able to take action against Bolt? Drivers / group action / regulators* 

{color:#bf2600}The drivers. {color}

*7. Is there any evidence the authorities have considered drivers eligible for employment benefits in the past (e.g. tax authorities, pension authorities etc)?*

{color:#bf2600}No.{color}

*8. What is the level of access to justice in a market (e.g. high state duties, requirement to have a representative etc)?*

{color:#bf2600}The labour jurisdiction allows anyone to represent themselves in court (meaning that legal representation is not mandatory) and there is no need to pay fees to file a claim.{color}

*9. Can claims be made to reclassify all drivers of the platform in a market at once?*

{color:#bf2600}No. Court rulings only have legal effects for the parties to the dispute. Therefore, no court ruling on illegal assignment would automatically apply to all drivers. {color}

----

Should you have any further questions/doubts, please do let me know.

